<title>USA: Palomar Q1 shr loss $0.50 vs loss $0.33.</title>
<headline>Palomar Q1 shr loss $0.50 vs loss $0.33.</headline>
<dateline>BEVERLEY, Mass. 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Amounts in thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>					   Three Months Ended</p>
<p>					  March 31     March 31</p>
<p>					    1997	  1996</p>
<p>Revenues			   $   20,126  $    6,925</p>
<p>Net (loss)			    (15,365)     (7,369)</p>
<p>Net (loss) per share		  (0.50)	(0.33)</p>
<p>Weighted-average number</p>
<p>of shares used in computation</p>
<p> of per-share net income	     31,037    22,239</p>
<p>NOTE: The company attributed its first quarter loss mainly to three factors: the minimal revenue effect of Food and Drug Administration clearance for its Epilaser hair removal system since it was announced with just three weeks left in the quarter; lower than anticipated volume from its electronics businesses; and start-up costs associated with our revenue-sharing business.</p>
<p>In addition, the company reserved an additional $2.5 million, or $0.11 per share, for possible costs associated with litigation matters.</p>
</text>
